<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Jesuits</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Jesuit</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Jesuits, or Society of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jesus">Jesus</a>, are a Catholic religious order founded in 1540. They were leading missionaries in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/asia">Asia</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/africa">Africa</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/americas">Americas</a>. Working under Portuguese patronage, they made many converts in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a> before <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/christianity">Christianity</a> was suppressed there, part of the impact of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/portuguese-empire">Portuguese Empire</a>.</p></div>
